      "finding": "Official operator migrate directly instantiates physical source/destination backends and copies encrypted data; a native sys/migrate refusal is not a substitute for checking that CLI contract or proof that this HTTP route is required.",
      "subject": "sys/migrate"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Present in old59 scope but absent from the exact default builtin plugin registry. May be an explicitly configured external-plugin or historical project requirement; do not count as default2.7.1 builtins from UI/client helper names alone.",
      "subject": "LDAP/RADIUS/Kerberos/OpenLDAP"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Current native EngineState explicitly admits SSH; a real typed native SSH owner and OTP lease methods exist. Do not reuse superseded old unsupported-SSH expectations as current gaps.",
      "subject": "SSH"
    }
  ],
  "implementation_principle": "Implement typed native owner, migration/cold codec, authorization, mandatory audit, revocation/renewal and unknown external-effect reconciliation before widening admission guards.",
